*>--- conformance-case
*> id: pb4893-interface-externalized-method-name
*> rules: [GR-14.9.23.4-2]
*> accept: [2002]
*> source-format: free
*>---
*> kb/Work PB4893: literal-1 names the method to invoke "as described in 8.3.2.2, User-defined words" (GR 2a), that is by
*> the name the method is externalized under, which is literal-1 of its METHOD-ID when one is written (11.7.4 GR 1b). The
*> interface prototype and its implementation are both METHOD-ID. PB4893GETX AS "PB4893GETY", so "PB4893GETY" selects the
*> method through a class-typed receiver, an interface-typed receiver and an inline invocation through the interface alike,
*> and each activation returns "0042", which the three DISPLAYs print.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
INTERFACE-ID. PB4893I.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
METHOD-ID. PB4893GETX AS "PB4893GETY".
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01 R PIC X(4).
PROCEDURE DIVISION RETURNING R.
END METHOD PB4893GETX.
END INTERFACE PB4893I.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
CLASS-ID. PB4893C INHERITS BASE.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
CONFIGURATION SECTION.
REPOSITORY.
    CLASS BASE
    INTERFACE PB4893I.
OBJECT. IMPLEMENTS PB4893I.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
METHOD-ID. PB4893GETX AS "PB4893GETY".
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01 R PIC X(4).
PROCEDURE DIVISION RETURNING R.
    MOVE "0042" TO R.
    GOBACK.
END METHOD PB4893GETX.
END OBJECT.
END CLASS PB4893C.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. PB4893P.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
CONFIGURATION SECTION.
REPOSITORY.
    CLASS PB4893C
    INTERFACE PB4893I.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 N PIC X(4) VALUE "0007".
01 C USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE PB4893C.
01 I USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE PB4893I.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-P.
    INVOKE PB4893C "NEW" RETURNING C.
    SET I TO C.
    INVOKE C "PB4893GETY" RETURNING N.
    DISPLAY N.
    MOVE "0007" TO N.
    INVOKE I "PB4893GETY" RETURNING N.
    DISPLAY N.
    MOVE "0007" TO N.
    MOVE I :: "PB4893GETY" TO N.
    DISPLAY N.
    STOP RUN.
END PROGRAM PB4893P.
